{
  "id": "p22",
  "title": "The Screen",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "p22-l1",
      "title": "clrscr and gotoxy",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "The PC's text screen has 80 columns and 25 rows. With uses crt, clrscr clears it, and gotoxy(x, y) puts the cursor anywhere: column x (1 to 80), row y (1 to 25). The next write starts there.",
        "Without gotoxy, text just scrolls up line by line, like on a Teletype. With it, a program can draw a whole screen: menus, forms, tables, even games.",
        "wherex and wherey tell you where the cursor is right now."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Title;",
          "uses crt;",
          "begin",
          "  clrscr;",
          "  gotoxy(30, 2);",
          "  write('TURBO PASCAL 3.0');",
          "  gotoxy(28, 3);",
          "  write('(C) 1983 Borland Inc.');",
          "  gotoxy(1, 6);",
          "  write('Press a key...');",
          "  writeln;",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": [
          "",
          "                             TURBO PASCAL 3.0",
          "                           (C) 1983 Borland Inc.",
          "",
          "",
          "Press a key..."
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
